# Maintainability & anti-slop

Prefer deepening existing seams over inventing parallel structure.
Goal: one place to change a behaviour; tokens, header flags, and shell-contract primitives stay single-sourced.

## Before you paste

When adding or extending behaviour, check the nearest sibling first.
If the change would clone a template, part, token map, header flag, or enqueue, extract or reuse a shared helper **before** adding the nth copy.

## Deepen, don't layer

Keep the runtime spine:

- **Tokens:** `theme.json` presets and `styles/**/*.json` variations that override the same slugs
- **Chrome and canvases:** `templates/` and `parts/` (header, footer, page/blog/404/search, `full-width`, `blank`)
- **Theme PHP:** `functions.php` for body class, recommend-plugin notice, and header-flag host
- **Theme CSS/JS:** only what `theme.json` cannot express (sticky, transparent, header-height token)

New behaviour goes into an existing cluster when one fits.
Do not add a second token system, a parallel header implementation, custom blocks, shortcodes, or a demo/Site Kit importer.

God-file rule of thumb: prefer extracting a coherent cluster (for example header flags) over growing `functions.php` or a catch-all CSS file with another pasted case.

**Deep** means lots of behaviour behind a small interface at a clear seam (tokens in `theme.json`, flags in one host).
**Shallow** means a pass-through wrapper whose interface is almost as complex as the implementation.
Prefer deepening an existing seam over adding another shallow module beside it.

## Single source for shared heuristics

Heuristics that exist in more than one place (token slugs, content/wide widths, header-height CSS, shell-contract primitive names) share one definition of truth.
Templates and parts reference only `theme.json` presets.
Do not hand-sync a second color, spacing, or width map "for convenience."

Ship or silence: do not advertise a header flag, canvas, or token in docs or copy unless the theme actually ships it.

## Completion check

Before finishing a change that adds a token, template, part, header flag, or shell-contract primitive: every list/map/template/`theme.json`/PRD surface that must know about it is updated, no phantom names remain, and no new duplicate helper was introduced beside an existing one.
Keep plugin territory (blocks, Design Library, Site Kit import, Global Design System writes) out of this theme.
